9},"\"",[306,830,403],{"class":389},[306,832,813],{"class":312},[306,834,835],{"class":316}," push\n",[243,837,838],{},"Kinotic OS reads entity definitions from the connected GitHub repository and synchronizes them for you -- publishing the entity creates the backing storage and registers its services. There is nothing to log in to or push from your machine besides git.",[247,840,842],{"id":841},"use-the-generated-repository","Use the Generated Repository",[243,844,845,846,849,850,853],{},"The provisioned repository ships a starter microservice at ",[292,847,848],{},"packages\u002Fmicroservices\u002Fmain"," that already sets the zone and connects. Extend its ",[292,851,852],{},"src\u002Fmain.ts"," to try the repository out:",[285,855,857],{"className":453,"code":856,"language":455,"meta":294,"style":294},"import { Kinotic, Pageable } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore'\nimport { PersistencePlugin } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fpersistence'\nimport { PersonRepository } from '@my-app\u002Fdomain'\nimport { appZone } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fmanagement-api'\nimport config from '..\u002F..\u002F..\u002F..\u002F.config\u002Fkinotic.config'\n\nKinotic.use(PersistencePlugin)\nKinotic.zonePrefix = appZone(config.organizationId, config.applicationId)\n\n\u002F\u002F server and credentials resolve from the environment: KINOTIC_SERVER_HOST\u002FPORT\u002FUSE_SSL,\n\u002F\u002F KINOTIC_CLIENT_ID\u002FKINOTIC_CLIENT_SECRET, which a deployment sets to the app server and the\n\u002F\u002F microservice's own machine identity. With nothing set it dials https:\u002F\u002Fapi.kinotic.ai, the org\n\u002F\u002F server, which admits no runtime\nawait Kinotic.connect()\n\nconst personRepository = new PersonRepository()\n\n\u002F\u002F Create a person\nconst person = await personRepository.save({\n    id: null,\n    firstName: 'Jane',\n    lastName: 'Doe',\n    age: 28\n})\n\nconsole.log('Saved:', person)\n\n\u002F\u002F Find all people\nconst page = await personRepository.findAll(Pageable.create(0, 10))